  "data": {
    "credits": {
      "intro": [
        "#Another killer game from some of the folks at NVision Design",
        " ",
        "It has been another crazy month at NVision Design.  The seasons have changed and so have we.",
        "NVD continues to be one of the top new media shops here in Dallas, as we sharpen our skills,",
        "add another year to our belt, and push the proverbial envelope.  In addition to the crew shown",
        "above, special thanks to the others at NVD: Dax, Don, Andy, Angel, Anna, Brian, Doug, Jacob,",
        "Jake, James, Janet, Lauren, Mark, Matthew, Mike, Michelle, Mollie, Nathan, Nick, Patrick,",
        "Risa, Vernon, Vertima, and Donna.",
        " ",
        "Thanks go out to those who truly are the *Pirates of the Silicon Prairie.*",
        " ",
        "#Click on any of the heads above to get additional credits and messages."
      ],
      "crewCredits": [
        [
          "#Michael *Bull* Bielinski - Initial Concept, Lead, C++ Programming",
          "Thanks to Ferg and Dax for being great business partners.  Thanks to the Frogapult fans",
          "and development team for pulling me out of a slump.  I'm back, Baby!!!  Where's Dan's ELO CD?",
          " ",
          "#Dan *Ferg* Ferguson - Creative Direction, Artwork, Concepting",
          "Thanks Mom, Dad, Leah, Lisa and all of my close friends for putting up with my antics. I'm going",
          "to be an uncle in a few days! It isn't work when I'm jammin' to Jason Faulkner, Tripping Daisy,",
          "Stereolab, Fat Boy Slim, The Freshmaka, Supergrass and Pavement! And thanks to Mike and Dax,",
          "two business partners that are my closest brothers. Hey Frito, bring back nacho cheese Cheetos!"
        ],
        [
          "#Matt *Worm* Johnson - Team Management, Concepting, Voice Talent, Storyline",
          "Worm would like to thank the whole NVD crew for their vision and dedication.  Without the",
          "countless hours of research, development and testing (hey... making the perfect",
          "frogImpaleSpikes.wav sound isn't easy!) none of this would be possible.  See you in 2000.",
          " ",
          "#Brandon *Broccoli Bite* Culpepper - Sound, Voice Talent, Testing",
          "I would like to thank Stephen, Andy, and Matt for helping me out with the elf sounds.",
          "I would also like to thank Molly and Anna for putting up with us screaming in the office."
        ],
        [
          "#Stephen *Sonic* Childs - Sound, Voice Talent, Testing",
          "Mom and Dad I love you; Andy, without you, I wouldn't know what the word friendship meant;",
          "Christina, thank you for patience and understanding and yes, I bought the screws!",
          " ",
          "#Detra *D* Jackson - Project Management and Coordination",
          "I would like to wish everyone a Merry Christmas",
          "and may they have a happy New Year!!!!"
        ],
        [
          "#Jason *Spud* Sutterfield - Scoreboard, Web and Database Integration",
          "I want to shout out to our X-Elf MFT, hey man, dont forget the second goal",
          "in being a One Minute Manager! And thanks to the cable company for screwing",
          "up my cable, allowing me ample time to get this project done!",
          " ",
          "#David *Frog Man* Vance - Web Design and Integration",
          "Thanks to all the NStormers who play NStorm games and the NVision Design team for creating",
          "another kick-ass game.  *We've talked about the future, and we've talked about the past,",
          "but tomorrow will be yesterday, so what will we do today?*"
        ],
        [
          "#Phil *Fill* Meadows - Web and Database Integration",
          "Thanks to my wife for putting up with me, Spud and Cameron for their help when I had a",
          "question, and everyone else at NVD, but especially, thanks to the guy who invented the widget",
          "in the bottom of the can of Guinness waiting for me at the end of each day! Happy Holidays!",
          " ",
          "#*Rickel the Pickel* Gonzales - Creative, Concepting",
          "Thanks to the Weirdheads for talking, drinking, and thinking with me."
        ]
      ],
      "headX": [195, 242, 137, 97, 151, 327, 36, 370, 82, 285],
      "headY": [67, 63, 43, 105, 110, 67, 82, 81, 53, 81]
    },
    "story": [
      "An Internet Christmas Story",
      " ",
      "'Twas the night before Christmas,",
      "and at the North Pole,",
      "Santa's sleigh was packed tight,",
      "the reindeer ready to go.",
      " ",
      "When out in the snow,",
      "there arose such a clatter,",
      "St. Nick sprang from the can,",
      "to see what was the matter.",
      " ",
      "\"The elves are on strike!\"",
      "cried Mrs. Claus with disdain.",
      "\"What shall we do, Santa?",
      "C'mon, rack your fat brain!\"",
      " ",
      "Santa's face began to sparkle,",
      "he shouted \"Merry Chistmas to All!\"",
      "He dashed to the coat closet,",
      "And grabbed his 16 pound ball.",
      " ",
      "Santa began to laugh so hard,",
      "His stomach was rolling,",
      "*Come on, you old woman,",
      "Its time for Elf Bowling...\"",
      " ",
      "Yes, Virginia...",
      "There really is Elf Bowling."
    ],
    "rules": [
      "The Official Elf Bowling Rules",
      " ",
      "Trouble brews in the Arctic north.  The recent",
      "explosion of online Christmas purchases has more",
      "than doubled the demand on the typically lazy",
      "workers of the ETMU (Elf Toy Makers Union).",
      " ",
      "Under the legal advice of Elliot Elf, the",
      "union's chief counsel, the elves have decided to",
      "strike against Santa's Workshop, Inc.",
      " ",
      "Upon hearing the news, President Claus knows",
      "there is only one way to resolve this conflict",
      "in time for Christmas... Elf Bowling!",
      " ",
      "Just press the space bar or click the mouse to",
      "stop the lane marker where you want Santa to aim",
      "his jolly ball.  Just like real bowling, you",
      "will get two chances per frame to knock the lazy",
